    "bio": "A Representative from Ohio; born in Niles, Trumbull County, Ohio, July 16, 1973; graduated from John F. Kennedy High School, Warren, Ohio, 1991; B.S., Bowling Green State University, Bowling Green, Ohio, 1995; J.D., Franklin Pierce Law Center, Rindge, N.H., 2000; staff, United States Representative James A. Traficant, Jr., of Ohio; member of the Ohio state senate, 2000-2002; elected as a Democrat to the One Hundred Eighth and to the nine succeeding Congresses (January 3, 2003-January 3, 2023); was not a candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Eighteenth Congress in 2022, but was an unsuccessful candidate for election to the United States Senate.",
